# Stage 6 right clamp (D-075 visibility rule; game-design.md Stage 6
# "Difficulty and reach rules"): the solver route with RIGHT added to every
# frame that doesn't hold LEFT, so through the whole scroll Resi's hitbox
# stays at the right clamp (its left edge 243-244 px right of the camera,
# 8 px short only around frame 1499) until her death at 4089. Measured on
# this replay (first frame any part of the enemy's hitbox is on screen ->
# first frame it reaches the clamp line, where she can be touched): swans
# #1-#3 63 frames (they trigger as soon as they are fully on screen, 20
# frames in, hiss 32, then charge; the sprite shows ~5 frames before the
# hitbox), Gelsen #1-#3 81 frames (60 frames hovering fully on screen,
# then the hunt), regatta boats #1-#3 85 frames (fully on screen 30 frames
# in, then the 60-frame start). Swans and Gelsen never touch her here (she
# dives under the swans as the solver does); regatta #1 bounces her off its
# masthead at 3827 (87 frames after it showed), and regatta #3, which she
# meets at the surface holding RIGHT, touches her at 4083 (87 frames after
# it showed) and kills her at 4089: the only death, by an enemy in view
# for > 60 frames.
level  = wolfgangsee
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = dies_at frames=4089..4089 deaths=1
